WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Transcriber: 

00:00:15.121 --> 00:00:22.121
(Plays Bach's "Cello Suite No. 1
in G Major, Prelude")

00:00:26.454 --> 00:00:33.163
(Plays The Piano Guys' "Cello Song")

00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:34.829
(Cheers and applause)

00:03:39.704 --> 00:03:40.954
(Applause ends)

00:03:43.038 --> 00:03:45.329
Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:03:45.371 --> 00:03:46.829
As Victor Borge used to say,

00:03:46.829 --> 00:03:50.788
"I'd like to thank my parents
for making this performance possible,

00:03:50.788 --> 00:03:53.288
and my children for making it necessary."

00:03:53.746 --> 00:03:55.204
(Laughter)

00:03:55.954 --> 00:04:00.496
So many people in our lives
make our life purpose possible --

00:04:00.538 --> 00:04:01.788
and necessary.

00:04:02.288 --> 00:04:04.288
I'd like to take you on a musical journey

00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:06.496
that connects you with
one of those people,

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.871
someone you love dearly,

00:04:08.913 --> 00:04:12.413
someone you wanted to have
a little more time to love,

00:04:12.454 --> 00:04:14.454
someone you wish was still with you.

00:04:15.579 --> 00:04:16.954
This is my mom.

00:04:17.788 --> 00:04:19.621
Isn't she beautiful?

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:23.996
And then there's this guy. (Clears throat)

00:04:24.038 --> 00:04:26.413
Yeah. I'm afraid that's me.

00:04:26.996 --> 00:04:31.954
Now, don't let that childlike grin
and superstylish Beatles haircut fool you:

00:04:31.996 --> 00:04:33.788
I was trouble.

00:04:33.788 --> 00:04:37.246
But as you could see,
I was happy when I was with my mom.

00:04:37.663 --> 00:04:41.246
She's one of the greatest
lyrical sopranos that's ever lived,

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:44.204
ineffably gifted
with the voice of an angel.

00:04:44.788 --> 00:04:48.454
She could have had center stage
anywhere -- anywhere in the world --

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:49.829
but she gave that up

00:04:50.788 --> 00:04:51.996
to be my mom.

00:04:52.496 --> 00:04:54.496
She gave me this stage with you today.

00:04:55.121 --> 00:04:57.871
She's been by my side
when I've been particularly nervous

00:04:57.871 --> 00:04:59.079
for a big performance,

00:04:59.079 --> 00:05:01.704
touring the world with The Piano Guys,

00:05:01.704 --> 00:05:03.246
or when I've been off the stage

00:05:03.246 --> 00:05:06.746
and struggling and at the mercy
of anxiety and depression.

00:05:07.704 --> 00:05:10.038
Or when I felt like I'm under the thumb

00:05:10.038 --> 00:05:14.496
of this perniciously pervasive demon
known as inadequacy

00:05:14.496 --> 00:05:16.038
that so many of us are fighting.

00:05:16.788 --> 00:05:19.621
She's gently nudged me forward

00:05:19.663 --> 00:05:22.913
right at the moment
when I've felt like giving up.

00:05:24.079 --> 00:05:28.163
So I'm a musician today, not only
because of what she gave up for me,

00:05:28.204 --> 00:05:31.038
but also because of what
she continues to give me.

00:05:32.246 --> 00:05:35.329
And that support is profound
and especially powerful.

00:05:35.329 --> 00:05:36.746
Why?

00:05:36.788 --> 00:05:41.663
Because it comes from a place
about which we know very little.

00:05:42.788 --> 00:05:45.788
Not long after that first picture
I showed you was taken,

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:52.579
my mother fell to the floor of our home
suddenly, in this really scary seizure.

00:05:53.579 --> 00:05:55.204
Such an intense moment.

00:05:55.246 --> 00:05:58.204
My dad rushed her to the ER:

00:05:58.246 --> 00:05:59.413
brain tumor.

00:06:01.246 --> 00:06:02.413
A big one.

00:06:03.454 --> 00:06:05.996
The doctors didn't know how long
we'd have with her --

00:06:06.038 --> 00:06:08.413
one, two, maybe three years
before we'd lose her.

00:06:09.454 --> 00:06:14.413
But due to her strength and a series
of indescribable miracles,

00:06:14.454 --> 00:06:17.579
she defied that prognosis
and fought that brain tumor

00:06:17.621 --> 00:06:20.121
for 18 years.

00:06:21.579 --> 00:06:22.621
(Applause)

00:06:22.663 --> 00:06:24.163
Thank you.

00:06:25.413 --> 00:06:26.996
I'll let her know. Thank you.

00:06:31.163 --> 00:06:34.079
She fought that brain tumor
for 18 years, but think about it:

00:06:34.079 --> 00:06:37.371
some of those years were really rough,
as you can imagine.

00:06:38.579 --> 00:06:41.454
But we learned to be grateful
for every day.

00:06:42.704 --> 00:06:46.788
Now, when her final curtain call came,
I couldn't applaud,

00:06:46.829 --> 00:06:48.954
because I wasn't ready for it to end.

00:06:49.954 --> 00:06:56.038
So after she passed away, I spent
some time being angry, bitter, resentful,

00:06:56.079 --> 00:06:58.871
confused at these years
that were stolen from me,

00:06:58.913 --> 00:07:03.288
at the chance I never had to know
the soprano in this beautiful woman;

00:07:04.579 --> 00:07:08.704
to hear her sing
in full voice without pain;

00:07:09.913 --> 00:07:12.371
to perform with her --
oh, I would have loved that,

00:07:12.371 --> 00:07:14.496
just me playing the cello
right next to her,

00:07:14.496 --> 00:07:16.704
just looking up
at her beautiful face singing.

00:07:16.746 --> 00:07:18.663
Oh, I would have loved that chance.

00:07:20.204 --> 00:07:21.621
I never got that chance.

00:07:22.329 --> 00:07:24.746
So I struggled with this, I really did.

00:07:24.788 --> 00:07:27.871
But then, I discovered something,

00:07:29.038 --> 00:07:32.204
something that has compelled me
to be on this stage,

00:07:32.246 --> 00:07:34.204
talking with you today.

00:07:35.579 --> 00:07:38.871
Isn't it true that our life's most
sublime melodies tend to be written

00:07:38.913 --> 00:07:41.163
during the dark symphonies
of our struggle?

00:07:42.746 --> 00:07:46.829
And in this dark symphony,
I found the healing for Mother --?

00:07:47.788 --> 00:07:52.579
The very thing that had wounded me
was the same thing that healed me:

00:07:53.829 --> 00:07:57.496
the power of music.

00:07:58.454 --> 00:08:03.163
You see, since then, I've spent
some very special time with my mom.

00:08:03.204 --> 00:08:04.996
Through music, I've discovered

00:08:05.038 --> 00:08:08.746
that the people we've lost
aren't lost at all,

00:08:08.746 --> 00:08:11.454
and the holes their absence
leaves inside us

00:08:11.496 --> 00:08:15.538
are not meant to be filled
by someone or something else.

00:08:17.371 --> 00:08:20.954
Instead, they are intentional,
mindful places,

00:08:20.996 --> 00:08:23.079
meant for us to go to take refuge,

00:08:23.079 --> 00:08:26.288
to reconnect and to reunite
with our loved ones,

00:08:26.288 --> 00:08:30.079
to find them there,
still interested, still invested

00:08:30.079 --> 00:08:34.704
and somehow, still involved
in the details of our lives.

00:08:36.371 --> 00:08:38.788
That is where I found my mom.

00:08:40.621 --> 00:08:43.371
Now, I can't prove this
to you with science;

00:08:43.413 --> 00:08:44.787
there's no chance.

00:08:45.787 --> 00:08:48.579
And spirituality helped me
take the first step,

00:08:48.621 --> 00:08:52.204
but ultimately, you just have to go there
yourself in your own way.

00:08:54.954 --> 00:08:59.496
And music, the power of music,
can act as a guide for you

00:08:59.537 --> 00:09:02.954
on this incredible, important journey.

00:09:03.787 --> 00:09:07.787
If you're willing,
I'd like to go there together right now.

00:09:07.787 --> 00:09:12.204
And I want to show this to you
because if you need to use this later on,

00:09:12.246 --> 00:09:14.246
when you're on your own in a quiet place,

00:09:14.246 --> 00:09:16.412
and you've got a song
that's personal to you,

00:09:16.412 --> 00:09:18.246
I want to show you how this can work.

00:09:19.162 --> 00:09:22.121
I'd like you to close your eyes
if you would, please.

00:09:23.454 --> 00:09:26.454
Choose a loved one
you want to connect with.

00:09:27.537 --> 00:09:31.204
It could be someone you've already been
thinking about as I've been talking.

00:09:31.662 --> 00:09:35.121
I want you to picture a favorite place,

00:09:35.121 --> 00:09:36.454
a relaxing place.

00:09:36.496 --> 00:09:39.704
It could be a place
that you both adored together.

00:09:42.287 --> 00:09:45.746
Now picture your loved one sitting
or standing across from you.

00:09:47.246 --> 00:09:49.746
Make this as detailed
as you can; it's important.

00:09:49.787 --> 00:09:50.954
What are they wearing?

00:09:51.996 --> 00:09:54.996
What is their posture, their expression?

00:09:56.204 --> 00:09:57.371
Is it a smile?

00:09:58.204 --> 00:09:59.662
Is it a look of concern?

00:10:00.329 --> 00:10:02.954
Or is hope written in their eyes?

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:07.079
I want you to hold
this image in your mind,

00:10:07.079 --> 00:10:09.662
and you could do so continually
with your eyes closed,

00:10:09.662 --> 00:10:11.496
or you can open them; it's up to you.

00:10:11.496 --> 00:10:13.246
But I want you to live in this place

00:10:13.287 --> 00:10:15.579
while I play for you
one more piece of music.

00:10:16.121 --> 00:10:18.454
It's a piece I've never
performed in public.

00:10:18.496 --> 00:10:21.412
Why? Because I feared
that I wouldn't do it justice.

00:10:23.246 --> 00:10:24.996
It's my mom's favorite.

00:10:26.371 --> 00:10:28.662
And as I play, I want you
to have a conversation

00:10:28.662 --> 00:10:30.704
with this beautiful person
across from you.

00:10:30.746 --> 00:10:34.621
I want you to hold their hand,
share a long hug,

00:10:36.496 --> 00:10:37.662
ask for forgiveness

00:10:37.704 --> 00:10:40.704
or finally give of it freely
if you need to.

00:10:41.662 --> 00:10:44.162
Ask for help with something
you're struggling with.

00:10:45.871 --> 00:10:50.454
At the very least, express gratitude
for how they've made you possible

00:10:51.412 --> 00:10:52.787
and necessary.

00:10:53.746 --> 00:10:55.121
Express love.

00:10:57.079 --> 00:10:59.662
My mother is a soprano,

00:11:02.371 --> 00:11:04.829
with the voice of an angel.

00:11:06.329 --> 00:11:08.246
And that voice for me is still sweet

00:11:08.287 --> 00:11:11.454
and rings with a resounding relevance.

00:11:13.412 --> 00:11:17.246
And as I play, I hope you can hear
the voice of your own angel

00:11:17.287 --> 00:11:22.454
and let music find someone you've lost.

00:11:38.496 --> 00:11:44.287
(Plays Puccini's "Nessun dorma")

00:12:18.787 --> 00:12:23.996
(Plays Puccini's "Nessun dorma")

00:13:12.704 --> 00:13:18.621
(Plays Puccini's "Nessun dorma")

00:13:45.037 --> 00:13:51.912
(Cheers and applause)

